      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1845 railroad developers founded the Belpre and Cincinnati Railroad, later renamed in 1851 when the line was redirected to Marietta.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belpre%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 7,140‑foot Parkersburg Bridge, completed in 1870, once stood as the world’s longest and brought Ohio coal to the East Coast.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        26,
        27,
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belpre%2C_Ohio",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Belpre sits on the Ohio River, directly opposite Parkersburg, West Virginia, about 14 miles downriver from Marietta.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
